Subject: [PATCH] Wire backend to DronaHQ's Event Management Agent for meeting
 requests
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Converse's policy already decides "advance_meeting" when a prospect asks
to meet (agents/converse/policy.py), but orchestrator/service.py never did
anything with that decision — no code ran, nothing was recorded.

Adds backend/integrations/dronahq_events.py, a real webhook client for the
team's DronaHQ "Event Management Agent" (the agent Sanchit built in DronaHQ
Studio that creates Google Calendar events and posts Slack/Gmail updates).
Wires it into process_converse(): an "advance_meeting" decision now sends a
natural-language meeting request to that agent and records its reply as a
conversation turn, instead of silently doing nothing.

Verified live end-to-end: the webhook call genuinely invokes the agent's
GPT-4o model and gets back a real, on-topic response.

Important caveat, documented in the module itself: DronaHQ has no native
SMS capability at all (checked the full Connector Library — no sms/twilio
tool exists), so this only covers the calendar/notification side; SMS
stays on integrations/sms.py (Twilio/Textbelt), added in the prior PR.
Also, the Event Management Agent's own tools (Google Calendar, Gmail,
Slack, Sheets, Twitter, LinkedIn) all show as unconnected in the DronaHQ
builder as of this commit -- someone with access to the team's Google/Slack
accounts needs to click "Connect" on each inside DronaHQ Studio before this
can actually create a calendar event or send a notification, rather than
just a conversational "please confirm the details" reply. That's a one-time
manual OAuth step in DronaHQ's UI, not something fixable in code.

